  "request": {
    "spec": "Terms now count business days. A claim's due-by is the terms-th business day after its date,\ncounting forward from the day after the claim's date and skipping every Saturday, Sunday and\nholiday on the sheet (so a claim dated on a Friday with terms 1 is due on the Monday, and a claim\nwith terms 5 is never due on a weekend or a holiday). Every due-by on the sheet is worked out this\nway, for the claims already on the sheet as well as new ones, each with the terms it was fixed with\nand the holidays on the sheet as this change arrives (a holiday added later still leaves an existing\ndue-by as it is); everything that reads the due-by (overdue, the late charge's\nboundaries, the period a claim belongs to) follows.\n",
    "prompt": "You are implementing ONE change to this application.\n\nFIRST read AGENTS.md \u2014 it states the working rules and how the app is tested, and sends you to\nDESIGN.md for the app's stack and conventions. Follow both.\n\nTHE CHANGE REQUEST:\nTerms now count business days. A claim's due-by is the terms-th business day after its date,\ncounting forward from the day after the claim's date and skipping every Saturday, Sunday and\nholiday on the sheet (so a claim dated on a Friday with terms 1 is due on the Monday, and a claim\nwith terms 5 is never due on a weekend or a holiday). Every due-by on the sheet is worked out this\nway, for the claims already on the sheet as well as new ones, each with the terms it was fixed with\nand the holidays on the sheet as this change arrives (a holiday added later still leaves an existing\ndue-by as it is); everything that reads the due-by (overdue, the late charge's\nboundaries, the period a claim belongs to) follows.\n\nYour work is verified by an automated Playwright UI test already installed under e2e/specs/.\nRead that spec: it declares the exact data-testid anchors, values, test data and any audit\nrecords it expects \u2014 match them. Run `bin/e2e` to build the app, start it, and run the test as\nyou work; iterate until it passes. Change whatever the request needs across the app \u2014 its stored\ndata, its server and its front end. Do NOT edit bin/build, bin/start, bin/stop, bin/e2e,\nAGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, DESIGN.md, e2e/support/ or the test spec.\n"
  },
